    "title": "The Masked Singer Season 14's Pugcasso's Care Bears Night Olympics Clue Explained (SPOILERS)",
    "text": "Image via FOX Published Mar 11, 2026, 9:00 PM EDT Lorianne Palinkas has been a reality television writer for Screen Rant for four years. After teaching middle school English for twenty years, she knows a thing or two about high drama, complicated alliances, and even singing competitions. Growing up in New York City gave her a solid foundation in the arts and culture. Sign in to your ScreenRant account WARNING! THIS ARTICLE CONTAINS MAJOR SPOILERS ABOUT THE MASKED SINGER SEASON 14!The Masked Singer season 14 introduced a new Olympics clue about Pugcasso, which could finally verify who he really is. Pugcasso has had four incredible performances so far, including \"Ordinary\" by Alex Warren (Premiere Night), \"Fake Plastic Tress\" by Radiohead (Clueless Night), \"Too Much\" by the Spice Girls (Spice Girls Night), and \"Dreams\" by The Cranberries (Care Bears Night). After his Care Bears Night performance, he advanced directly into the semi-finals. So far, the Masked Singer panelists have been completely stumped by Pugcasso, guessing that he was Dan Reynolds, Rob Thomas or Pat Monahan (Ken Jeong); Darren Criss, Charlie Puth, or Jason Mraz (Rita Ora); Gavin DeGraw or Vance Joy (Jenny McCarthy-Wahlberg); and Ryan Tedder or Jack Johnson (Robin Thicke). However, they're most likely incorrect because all of Pugcasso's clues point to singer and American Idol season 11 winner Phillip Phillips. Credit: Trae Patton / FOX During The Masked Singer season 14 Care Bears Night, Pugcasso revealed, \"This isn't my first competition. I've even taken the Olympics by storm.\" A clue featuring the Olympic torch was then revealed. After his performance, Pugcasso explained, \"Being a part of the Olympics ... it changed my life forever. So, I never imagined I'd have the whole world's attention. So it was a pretty cool moment.\" Related This wasn't the only reference to Pugcasso and Phillip's connection to the Olympics during The Masked Singer season 14. On Premiere Night, one of his clues was London's Big Ben. London is where the Olympics took place when Phillip's song was featured. Other Clues That Prove Pugcasso Is Phillip Phillips Pugcasso also mentioned being rejected by people who told him that he wasn't good at music. Phillip auditioned for America's Got Talent season 2 before American Idol, but he didn't make it to the finals, and his appearance wasn't aired on the show. During The Masked Singer season 14 Spice Girls Night, Pugcasso told a story about doing the biggest show of his life in another country, surrounded by music legends Bruce Springsteen and John Mayer. In 2013, Phillip toured with John Mayer, and, as part of the tour, he sang at the Rock in Rio festival in Rio de Janeiro, Brazil. Bruce Springsteen and the E Street Band also performed there. A Hawaiian shirt on Clueless Night was a hint about Phillip's appearance in an episode of Hawaii Five-0. A golf clue referred to his love for the game and his participation in celebrity golf tournaments. Although it hasn't been confirmed yet, all of Pugcasso's clues indicate that he's most likely Phillip. His latest Olympics clue is further confirmation of this. The panelists aren't even close to guessing him, and he's so talented that fans will most likely have to wait until the Masked Singer season 14 finale to see if this guess is right. Whoever Pugcasso turns out to be, he has a fantastic chance of taking home the Golden Mask Trophy because he's a true artist. The Masked Singer airs Wednesdays at 8 p.m. ET on FOX.",
